#: ../guide/concepts.md:56 7b70b83417cc4afd9fa57f758de20069
msgid "Order"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/concepts.md:58 a46c9926d44b483bb06fb73624cd1b65
msgid ""
"A trade *intention* — what you'd like to do. Created with a signed size "
"(positive = buy, negative = sell), optional `limit` / `stop` / `sl` / "
"`tp` / `tag`, and an `asset` symbol. Orders go through the broker's "
"queues and either fill or get rejected (typically for insufficient "
"margin)."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/concepts.md:63 5c0a2b48e69e42eab9c849c795c33d65
msgid "Trade"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/concepts.md:65 687bb250291f46e39b7ce31640ac30cf
msgid ""
"A *filled* position. Each Order that fills opens (or partially closes) a "
"Trade. While open, the Trade has `entry_price`, `entry_date`, `size`, "
"optional `sl` / `tp`. When the Trade is closed (by an opposite-side "
"order, an SL/TP trigger, or end-of-backtest), it gets `exit_price`, "
"`exit_date`, `profit`, and an `exit_reason`."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/concepts.md:71 b99da8912c50445a8f54137c997cd77b
msgid "Position"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/concepts.md:73 01402da0d4884057874fba94b73887c1
msgid ""
"A holder for trades on one asset. `active_trades` are open; "
"`closed_trades` are closed. `position.size` is the net signed size across"
" all active trades on that asset."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/concepts.md:77 66e13c4b7d5041a5865a6a3c00801f4a
msgid ""
"For multi-asset, the Broker holds `positions: dict[str, Position]` — one "
"per asset. `broker.position` (singular) is a convenience accessor that "
"only works in single-asset mode."
msgstr ""

